 "text": "Quarterly Service Report\nHarbor Valley Water District\nService figures, July to September 2026\nThe district served more homes this quarter than in any quarter before, and fixed leaks faster. The figures below are\ncounted by area, from the work orders closed by the end of September.\nArea\nHomes served\nLeaks fixed\nHours without water\nSamples passed\nBill change\nNorth\n6,420|\n48\n3.5\n100%\n+0.0%\nEast\n8,115\n61\n4.0|\n100%\n-1.2%\nSouth\n5,980 |\n37\n2.5\n99.6%\n+0.0%\nWest\n4,760\n52|\n6.5\n100%\n+0.8%\nMill Road\n2,305\n19\n1.0\n100%\n-2.5%\nCedar Avenue\n1,890|\n14\n4 |\n1.5 |\n100%\n+0.0% \nAll areas\n29,470 |\n231\n3.8\n99.9%\n-0.4%\nTable 1. Service by area in the third quarter of 2026.\nCrew hours by month\nMost hours went to planned repairs. Emergency calls fell in each month of the quarter.\nMonth\nRepairs\nInspections\nEmergencies\nTotal\nJuly\n1,240\n380\n96 |\n1,716\nAugust\n1,315\n410\n71 |\n1,796\nSeptember\n1,190\n455\n58 |\n1,703\nQuarter\n3,745 |\n1,245\n225|\n5,215\nTable 2. Crew hours, by the kind of work and by month.\nharborvalleywater.example\nPage 2\n",
 "html": "<header><p>Quarterly Service Report</p></header>\n<header><p>Harbor Valley Water District</p></header>\n<h2>Service figures, July to September 2026</h2>\n<p>The district served more homes this quarter than in any quarter before, and fixed leaks faster. The figures below are counted by area, from the work orders closed by the end of September.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><td>Area</td><td>Homes served</td><td>Leaks fixed</td><td>Hours without water</td><td>Samples passed</td><td>Bill change</td></tr>\n<tr><td>North</td><td>6,420|</td><td>48</td><td>3.5</td><td>100%</td><td>+0.0%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>East</td><td>8,115</td><td>61</td><td>4.0|</td><td>100%</td><td>-1.2%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>South</td><td>5,980 |</td><td>37</td><td>2.5</td><td>99.6%</td><td>+0.0%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>West</td><td>4,760</td><td>52|</td><td>6.5</td><td>100%</td><td>+0.8%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Mill Road</td><td>2,305</td><td>19</td><td>1.0</td><td>100%</td><td>-2.5%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cedar Avenue</td><td>1,890|</td><td>14 4 |</td><td>1.5 |</td><td>100%</td><td>+0.0% </td></tr>\n<tr><td>All areas</td><td>29,470 |</td><td>231</td><td>3.8</td><td>99.9%</td><td>-0.4%</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Table 1. Service by area in the third quarter of 2026.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<h2>Crew hours by month</h2>\n<p>Most hours went to planned repairs. Emergency calls fell in each month of the quarter.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><td>Month</td><td>Repairs</td><td>Inspections</td><td>Emergencies</td><td>Total</td></tr>\n<tr><td>July</td><td>1,240</td><td>380</td><td>96 |</td><td>1,716</td></tr>\n<tr><td>August</td><td>1,315</td><td>410</td><td>71 |</td><td>1,796</td></tr>\n<tr><td>September</td><td>1,190</td><td>455</td><td>58 |</td><td>1,703</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Quarter</td><td>3,745 |</td><td>1,245</td><td>225|</td><td>5,215</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Table 2. Crew hours, by the kind of work and by month.</td><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</table>\n<footer><p>harborvalleywater.example</p></footer>\n<footer><p>Page 2</p></footer>\n"
